--- reading it
    1xQ (1 reference, 10 queries) and Nx1 (100 references, 1 query) are independent, so
    those two rows separate query-side from reference-side cost: whichever is larger
    dominates its side. NxQ is the full grid at 1000 cells, and per-cell cost should
    match the two single-sided rows. Cost falling per cell with the count is fixed
    per-invocation cost being amortised, not a scaling penalty. Peak RSS is a per-process
    high-water mark.

